  "lesson": "## Two copies, one endless first beat\n\nThe same break on both decks, hot cue 1 on its first beat. Play A's one, and two beats later cut to B and press B1 so the room hears the first two beats again; two beats later back to A. The break's first half repeats forever. From bar 5 the cut comes every beat, so only the downbeat is left.\n\nThis is beat juggling as Wikipedia and School of Scratch describe it: extending a section by alternating between two copies. The cue press restarts the copy that is silent, the crossfader reveals it, and both must be on the beat. You need the audio to hear whether the juggle is seamless; the scorer checks that the cue and the cut are one event.\n",
